                'needs_review' => false,
            ],
            [
                'text' => 'What happens to a ship\'s Center of Gravity (G) when a crane lifts a 50 MT weight off the jetty or hold bottom?',
                'category' => 'technical',
                'duration_seconds' => 90,
                'note' => 'The exact instant the weight clears the deck or jetty, its center of gravity jumps instantaneously to the head of the crane jib (point of suspension), causing an immediate virtual rise in KG and loss of GM.',
