            [
                'text' => 'How do you load a small parcel of cargo so that the Draft Aft remains completely unchanged?',
                'category' => 'technical',
                'duration_seconds' => 120,
                'note' => 'Load the cargo at a distance x forward of the Centre of Flotation (F) such that the bodily sinkage at the aft perpendicular is exactly cancelled by the trim effect: x = (MCTC × L) / (TPC × la), where L = length between perpendiculars and la = distance of F from the aft perpendicular. Loading further forward than x lifts the stern; loading less far forward increases the aft draught.',
